      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure about this part. available() on an L2CAP socket is useful when trying to drop the rest of the packet which isn\u0027t otherwise possible. Usually, a partial read to a SOCK_SEQPACKET or SOCK_DGRAM drops the unread bytes. However, due to the presence of mL2capBuffer, this is not the case for L2CAP sockets.\nIt looks like the javadocs for InputStream#available would allow for an implementation that just does:\n`return mL2capBuffer.remaining()`\n\nThat being said, I don\u0027t know how apps use this API today and whether this wouldn\u0027t break some of them.",
